{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he shall take a full censer.</b> For immediately, once the sin-offering is slaughtered and confession made and iniquity removed, one becomes prepared to enter the light in the light of the King's face. And behold, the King appears to all who are prepared for His light, as it says: כִּי בֶּעָנָן אֵרָאֶה (Leviticus 16:2). And it is fitting to honor Him with incense, like the practice after the daily offerings, as it says: עֹלַת תָּמִיד לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם פֶּתַח אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד אֲשֶׁר אִוָּעֵד לָכֶם שָׁמָּה (Exodus 29:42). In this matter the sons of Aaron erred, and they offered what He had not commanded them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:38.436514749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}